WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.474
Danny: Whoo boy! This is going to be good.

2
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:13.275
Brad: I just have to connect this wire to the battery . . .

3
00:00:13.276 --> 00:00:14.981
There, that's it.

4
00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:17.112
Danny: Will it work?

5
00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:22.322
Brad: Yes, if, as I expect, the nano-putty causes things to

6
00:00:22.323 --> 00:00:27.530
shrink. Danny: It says so on the

7
00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:30.319
box! Brad: Well, I guess it should work

8
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:41.681
then. Danny: Let's try

9
00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:44.586
it! What about Tabby over there?

10
00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:48.196
Brad: No! What if . . . what if something went wrong?

11
00:00:48.197 --> 00:00:50.207
Danny: Nothing will go wrong.

12
00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.332
You said it would work.

13
00:00:52.333 --> 00:01:02.535
Brad: Well, yes. Nothing should go wrong . .

14
00:01:02.536 --> 00:01:06.617
. Let's test it on something that isn't alive.

15
00:01:06.618 --> 00:01:09.854
Danny: Fine.

16
00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:14.651
Brad: What about . . . that umbrella?

17
00:01:14.652 --> 00:01:24.066
Danny: That's boring. But sure, go ahead.

18
00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.597
Brad: Something happened!

19
00:01:26.598 --> 00:01:30.608
Danny: I still can't see . . .

20
00:01:30.609 --> 00:01:36.245
Brad: It's . . . I think I see . . . oh my!

21
00:01:36.246 --> 00:01:41.447
Danny: Wow!

22
00:01:41.448 --> 00:01:43.352
What went wrong?

23
00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:44.774
Brad: I don't know.

24
00:01:44.775 --> 00:01:49.092
Ah! The nano-streams must be crossed.

25
00:01:49.093 --> 00:01:51.742
Danny: So, instead of shrinking it . . .

26
00:01:51.743 --> 00:01:57.834
Brad: It made it bigger.

27
00:01:57.836 --> 00:02:00.335
What should we try it on next? Danny:

28
00:02:00.336 --> 00:02:05.786
I still think the cat is a good idea. Brad:

29
00:02:05.787 --> 00:02:07.661
How about that plant? It's

30
00:02:07.662 --> 00:02:11.304
a living thing, but it's not my pet. Danny:

31
00:02:11.305 --> 00:02:17.661
Let me do it this time!

32
00:02:17.662 --> 00:02:19.466
Brad: That was better.

33
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:25.001
Danny: There was less smoke this time.

34
00:02:25.002 --> 00:02:27.973
Brad: It's got polka dots.

35
00:02:27.974 --> 00:02:31.965
Danny: It's not smaller at all.

36
00:02:31.967 --> 00:02:35.078
I don't think this nano-putty works! Brad:

37
00:02:35.079 --> 00:02:38.504
If my dad invented it, it works. Maybe

38
00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:41.606
I'm not doing something right. Danny:

39
00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:47.997
Still, it would be funny if the bullies were covered in polka dots.

40
00:02:47.998 --> 00:02:53.630
Hee-hee! They'd try to wash the dots off, but they wouldn't come off! Brad:

41
00:02:53.631 --> 00:02:55.527
Oops! Danny:

42
00:02:55.528 --> 00:02:56.829
What? Brad:

43
00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:04.322
I think this accidentally got in to the gun. Danny:

44
00:03:04.323 --> 00:03:06.459
How did that get in there? Brad:

45
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.769
I don't know. Danny:

46
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:13.665
You use pink polka-dotted Band-Aids? Ha-ha! Brad:

47
00:03:13.666 --> 00:03:15.514
I cut my finger. It

48
00:03:15.515 --> 00:03:18.677
was the only one I could find.

49
00:03:18.678 --> 00:03:22.919
Danny: Ha-ha! That's a Band-Aid for a baby girl!

50
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.490
Brad: Don't laugh.

51
00:03:24.491 --> 00:03:27.928
Danny: Oooh. Did your mommy kiss it better?

52
00:03:27.929 --> 00:03:39.614
Brad: Stop teasing! No wonder the bullies don't like you.

